# graphify-specific exclusions (gitignore syntax) — content that's tracked in
# git (so .gitignore doesn't touch it) but isn't application code/architecture
# docs, and pollutes query/explain results with the tool's own self-referential
# output when ingested as if it were part of the codebase.

# This repo's own graphify-vs-docs experiment write-ups: natural-language prose
# *about* graphify itself (queries run, plan comparisons, judged scores). When
# ingested, terms like "Critical", "Judge's scores", "Results" surface as
# false-positive matches for unrelated real-code queries. Real architectural
# decisions from this work already live in docs/architecture/ and docs/plans/,
# which are not excluded here.
docs/experiments/

# The `impeccable` design-critique skill's own generated report output
# (timestamped critique markdown files) — tool-generated artifacts, not
# authored documentation, analogous to graphify's own graphify-out/.
.impeccable/
